      "introduction": "Run the drills before any graded work. Ten minutes at the start of every session, filling a ruled A4 box with parallel shoulder lines and then with lines converging to a marked point, changes the hand within three weeks. Judge each sheet by sighting along it rather than by looking at it flat, and check three things only: does the line arrive in one pass, is the spacing even across the middle, and does the end of the stroke stop cleanly without a hook. Name the four variables of every line as you draw, grade, edge, speed and pressure, so that the effect becomes intentional instead of accidental.",
