          "content": "A constructed line is produced with an instrument, and it is measured, parallel, tapered or repeated to a rule. It belongs to graphic layout, technical projection and the geometry of a kente or lettering grid, where an edge that wanders is a failure of the whole panel. An expressive line is drawn freehand and is judged by the feeling it carries: a broken, pressing line suggests rusted thatch or a crusted wall, a long whip of a line suggests the speed of a trotro running the Accra road, a heavy trembling line suggests weight or age. Both are tools, and candidates lose marks by confusing them, because an expressive question that demands mood punishes a ruled answer while a perspective construction punishes a wobbling freehand. Everything about line character is controlled by four variables only: the grade of pencil, the edge of the lead, the speed of the stroke and the pressure behind it. Naming which variable produces which effect is the difference between drawing by accident and drawing by intention.",
