          "keyTakeaway": "A technical drawing is read through its line code before it is read through its shapes; keep each type doing one job.",
          "realWorldExample": "A fabricator at the Abossey Okai spare-parts cluster reads a bracket print whose mounting holes are shown by centre lines and dashed depths, so he drills the blind holes to the right depth without guessing."
